          },
          "author": "Yoto",
          "description": "When Vivian, the gifted daughter of garlic farmers, wins Transylvania's Got Talent with her outstanding violin playing, she is given the opportunity of a lifetime: the chance to play first chair in the world-famous Johann Sebastian Bach's orchestra! But after being whisked away to Castle Bachula, where Bach's Children of the Night live and practice, Vivian quickly learns that things aren't quite what they seem. With some help from the leader of the local wolf pack, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Vivian shows the musical world that a little change can go a long way.\n\nPerfect for Halloween fans and parties. Listeners of all ages will love this spooky hip-hopera based on classical works by Bach and Mozart, re-imagined by Secret Agent 23 Skidoo for Yoto.",
